  <section xml:id="sec-pre-assignment-nov-24">
    <title>Tue Nov 24: Arc Length and Surface Area</title>
    <p>
      Today in class: <xref ref="sec-8-1-arc-length" text="title"/> (Stewart 8.1 and 8.2).
    </p>
    <assemblage>
      <title>Think about this</title>
      <p>How long is a curvy road? You can measure straight lines easily.</p>
      <p>Could lots of tiny straight pieces do the job?</p>
    </assemblage>
    <p>
      <alert>Link coming soon.</alert> The Doenet warm-up will appear here before class.
      About 10 minutes, completion credit.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section xml:id="sec-pre-assignment-dec-01">
    <title>Tue Dec 1: Fluid Pressure and Center of Mass</title>
    <p>
      Today in class: <xref ref="sec-8-3-applications-physics-engineering" text="title"/> (Stewart 8.3).
    </p>
    <assemblage>
      <title>Think about this</title>
      <p>Why is a dam built thicker at the bottom than at the top?</p>
      <p>And where would you put your finger to balance a flat, oddly shaped plate?</p>
    </assemblage>
    <p>
      <alert>Link coming soon.</alert> The Doenet warm-up will appear here before class.
      About 10 minutes, completion credit.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section xml:id="sec-pre-assignment-dec-03">
